# Rapid Design System — Agent Rules

## What This Is
A design token pipeline. JSON tokens in → CSS variables, utility classes, and framework adapters out. One source of truth for every UI library. No runtime JS theming — dark mode is pure CSS via `data-theme` attribute.

## The Golden Rule
Every colour, spacing, font, radius, shadow, opacity, duration, and z-index value in the system traces back to `tokens/base.json`. If it's not in the JSON, it doesn't exist in the system. Never hardcode values in adapters or CSS — always reference `var(--rapid-*)`.

## File Map (what generates what)

```
tokens/base.json ─────────┐
tokens/dark.json ─────────┤
tokens/local.json* ───────┤  * optional
tokens/themes/*.json* ────┤
                          ▼
        scripts/build-tokens.js (npm run build)
                          │
        ┌─────────────────┼──────────────────────┐
        ▼                 ▼                      ▼
  packages/css/      packages/fluent-*/     packages/adapters/
  global.css         index.ts              bootstrap5.css
  utilities.css      Provider.tsx          ag-grid.css
  scoped-overrides   (v8 + v9)            chartjs.ts
                                           ... (15 total)
```

**NEVER edit files in `packages/`** — they are auto-generated. Edit the builder functions in `scripts/build-tokens.js` instead.

## How To Add a Token

1. Add to `tokens/base.json` (nested JSON path becomes hyphenated CSS var name)
2. Add dark override to `tokens/dark.json` (only if value differs in dark mode)
3. Run `npm run build`
4. The token automatically gets: CSS variable in `global.css`, utility classes in `utilities.css`, Tailwind preset entry

Example: `{ "color": { "accent": { "coral": "#ff6b6b" } } }` → `--rapid-color-accent-coral`

## How To Add an Adapter

Every adapter is a function in `scripts/build-tokens.js` that returns a string.

Pattern for CSS variable override adapters:
```js
function buildMyLibAdapter() {
  return `${fileHeader("My Library Adapter", [
    "Description of what this maps.",
    "Load AFTER the library's own CSS.",
  ])}

:root {
  --lib-bg: ${v("color-surface-base")};
  --lib-text: ${v("color-text-primary")};
  --lib-border: ${v("color-border-default")};
  --lib-primary: ${v("color-brand-primary")};
  --lib-font: ${v("font-family-base")};
}
`;
}
```

Then register in `main()`:
```js
emit(path.join(ADAPTERS_DIR, "my-lib.css"), buildMyLibAdapter());
```

And add to `package.json` exports:
```json
"./adapters/my-lib.css": "./packages/adapters/my-lib.css"
```

For JS bridge adapters (canvas libraries), import from `_css-vars-bridge.ts` and use `token()`, `palette()`, `onThemeChange()`.

## How To Add a Utility Class

Edit `buildUtilitiesCSS()` in `scripts/build-tokens.js`. Follow the existing pattern — iterate over flattened token entries, generate a class per token. Use `var()` references, never raw values.

## Helper Functions in build-tokens.js

- `v("token-key")` → `var(--rapid-token-key)` — use in adapter templates
- `toCSSVar("key")` → `--rapid-key` — raw CSS property name
- `flatten(obj, prefix)` → `[["prefix-key", "value"], ...]` — flattens nested JSON
- `fileHeader(title, extraLines)` → standard comment block for generated files
- `emit(path, content)` → write file + log
- `sanitizeCSSValue(val)` → validates CSS value safety (rejects `;{}`)
- `validateTokenKey(key)` → validates CSS identifier safety
- `deepMerge(target, source)` → recursive merge with prototype pollution guard

## Security Invariants

- Every object iteration MUST skip `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` (use `isSafeKey()` or check `UNSAFE_KEYS`)
- Every CSS value emitted MUST pass through `sanitizeCSSValue()`
- Every CSS key emitted MUST pass through `validateTokenKey()`
- Never use `innerHTML` in the demo page — use `createElement` + `textContent`
- Never interpolate user input into HTML attributes without validation
- JSON.parse calls MUST be wrapped in try/catch

## CSS Variable Naming Convention

`--rapid-{category}-{subcategory}-{name}`

Derived from JSON path: `{ "color": { "brand": { "primary": "#0f6cbd" } } }` → `--rapid-color-brand-primary`

## Utility Class Naming Convention

- Colors: `.rapid-bg-{slug}`, `.rapid-text-{slug}`, `.rapid-border-{slug}`
- Spacing: `.rapid-p-{size}`, `.rapid-px-{size}`, `.rapid-m-{size}`, `.rapid-mt-{size}`, etc.
- Radius: `.rapid-rounded-{size}`
- Shadow: `.rapid-shadow-{size}`
- Typography: `.rapid-text-size-{size}`, `.rapid-font-{weight}`, `.rapid-leading-{name}`, `.rapid-tracking-{name}`
- Opacity: `.rapid-opacity-{name}`
- Z-index: `.rapid-z-{name}`
- Duration: `.rapid-duration-{name}`

Note: text color tokens strip the `text-` prefix to avoid `.rapid-text-text-primary`. The slug for `color.text.primary` is `primary`, not `text-primary`.

## Semantic Aliasing

Token values starting with `$` reference other tokens by dot-path:
```json
{ "color": { "action": { "primary": "$color.brand.primary" } } }
```
Resolved at build time by `resolveAliases()`.

## Named Themes

JSON files in `tokens/themes/*.json` compile to `[data-theme="filename"]` CSS blocks. The filename (without .json) becomes the attribute value.

## Verification After Changes

```bash
npm run build                    # must succeed, outputs 22+ artefacts
npm run check:contrast           # flags accessibility issues
npm run audit -- ./demo          # check token adoption
```

## npm Scripts Reference

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `build` | Compile all tokens → CSS + adapters |
| `check:contrast` | WCAG 2.1 contrast audit |
| `audit` | Token usage governance report |
| `sync:figma` | Pull from Figma Variables API |
| `sync` | Pull from Figma + build |
| `import:tokens-studio` | Transform Tokens Studio export |
| `generate:dark` | Auto-derive dark.json from base.json |
| `export:native` | Generate React Native / iOS / Android tokens |
| `demo` | Serve interactive playground |

## Do NOT

- Edit files in `packages/` directly (they're generated)
- Use JavaScript/React context for theme switching (use `data-theme` attribute)
- Hardcode colour/spacing values in adapters (use `v("token-key")`)
- Add component UI code (RDS is infrastructure, not components)
- Use `innerHTML` in the demo page
- Skip prototype pollution guards in object iteration
- Ship `scripts/`, `demo/`, or `.figmarc*` in the npm package
